,2,[288,299,300],{},"  L[Ligne de log, \u002Fproc, Redis] -->|agent| E[Wolf Event \u002F Wolf Metric Sample]\n",[288,302,304],{"class":290,"line":303},3,[288,305,306],{},"  S[Hooks du site] --> E\n",[288,308,310],{"class":290,"line":309},4,[288,311,312],{},"  E -->|règle, chaque minute| I[Wolf Incident]\n",[288,314,316],{"class":290,"line":315},5,[288,317,318],{},"  I -->|ouverture, réouverture, résolution| C[Canaux]\n",[320,321,322,334,348,359],"ol",{},[323,324,325,326,329,330,333],"li",{},"L'",[224,327,328],{},"agent"," analyse les logs et lit l'état du système. Il envoie des événements et des\néchantillons de métriques toutes les ",[233,331,332],{},"push_interval"," (30 s).",[323,335,336,337,339,340,343,344,347],{},"Le ",[224,338,226],{}," les stocke. Les événements qui ont la même empreinte sont comptés sur une seule\nligne (",[224,341,342],{},"Nombre",", ",[224,345,346],{},"Vu pour la dernière fois",") au lieu de s'accumuler.",[323,349,350,351,354,355,358],{},"Chaque minute, chaque ",[224,352,353],{},"règle d'alerte"," lit sa fenêtre. Quand sa condition est remplie, elle\nouvre un ",[224,356,357],{},"incident"," par groupe, ou alimente l'incident déjà ouvert.",[323,360,361,362,365],{},"L'incident prévient ses ",[224,363,364],{},"canaux"," à son ouverture, à sa réouverture, à son escalade et à sa\nrésolution, jamais à chaque événement.",[188,367,369],{"id":368},"les-objets","Les objets",[197,371,372,382],{},[200,373,374],{},[203,375,376,379],{},[206,377,378],{},"DocType",[206,380,381],{},"Contenu",[216,383,384,427,454,470,503,513,522],{},[203,385,386,391],{},[221,387,388],{},[224,389,390],{},"Wolf Event",[221,392,393,394,343,397,343,400,343,403,343,406,343,409,412,413,416,417,343,420,343,423,426],{},"Quelque chose qui s'est produit : ",[233,395,396],{},"error",[233,398,399],{},"cron_failure",[233,401,402],{},"worker_failure",[233,404,405],{},"security",[233,407,408],{},"host_metric_alert",[233,410,411],{},"deployment",". Possède une catégorie (par exemple ",[233,414,415],{},"web_attack_probe","), une gravité (",[233,418,419],{},"info",[233,421,422],{},"warning",[233,424,425],{},"critical","), un périmètre, un compteur et une charge utile JSON.",[203,428,429,434],{},[221,430,431],{},[224,432,433],{},"Wolf Metric Sample",[221,435,436,437,343,440,343,443,446,447,450,451,453],{},"Une valeur d'une métrique (",[233,438,439],{},"cpu_usage",[233,441,442],{},"http_502",[233,444,445],{},"tls_days_left","…) pour un périmètre à un instant donné. Agrégée dans ",[224,448,449],{},"Wolf Metric Rollup"," par minute et par heure. Voir ",[270,452,168],{"href":169},".",[203,455,456,461],{},[221,457,458],{},[224,459,460],{},"Wolf Alert Rule",[221,462,463,467,468,453],{},[464,465,466],"em",{},"Quand X > Y pendant Z minutes, envoyer une alerte."," Signal, agrégation, fenêtre, regroupement, canaux. Voir ",[270,469,91],{"href":92},[203,471,472,477],{},[221,473,474],{},[224,475,476],{},"Wolf Incident",[221,478,479,480,343,483,486,487,490,491,343,494,343,497,500,501,453],{},"Des événements qui partagent une cause, pour un groupe d'une règle. Statut ",[224,481,482],{},"Ouvert",[224,484,485],{},"Acquitté"," ou ",[224,488,489],{},"Résolu"," (",[233,492,493],{},"Open",[233,495,496],{},"Acknowledged",[233,498,499],{},"Resolved"," dans l'API). Lié au déploiement qui l'a précédé. Voir ",[270,502,106],{"href":107},[203,504,505,510],{},[221,506,507],{},[224,508,509],{},"Wolf Silence",[221,511,512],{},"Une fenêtre de maintenance : les incidents s'ouvrent toujours, les notifications attendent.",[203,514,515,519],{},[221,516,517],{},[224,518,35],{},[221,520,521],{},"Un hôte enregistré, un site satellite ou une intégration, avec son dernier envoi et son décalage d'horloge.",[203,523,524,529],{},[221,525,526],{},[224,527,528],{},"Wolf Settings",[221,530,531],{},"Rétention, signaux, agents, export SIEM, renseignement sur les menaces.",[188,533,535],{"id":534},"gravité","Gravité",[193,537,538],{},"Chaque gravité a une couleur et une forme, pour ne jamais dépendre de la couleur seule :",[197,540,541,553],{},[200,542,543],{},[203,544,545,547,550],{},[206,546,535],{},[206,548,549],{},"Symbole",[206,551,552],{},"Signification",[216,554,555,567,579,591],{},[203,556,557,561,564],{},[221,558,559],{},[233,560,419],{},[221,562,563],{},"○",[221,565,566],{},"Bon à savoir.",[203,568,569,573,576],{},[221,570,571],{},[233,572,422],{},[221,574,575],{},"◐",[221,577,578],{},"À regarder dans la journée.",[203,580,581,585,588],{},[221,582,583],{},[233,584,425],{},[221,586,587],{},"●",[221,589,590],{},"Quelqu'un est réveillé.",[203,592,593,596,599],{},[221,594,595],{},"resolved",[221,597,598],{},"✓",[221,600,601],{},"Retour à la normale.",[188,603,605],{"id":604},"déploiements","Déploiements",[193,607,608,609,611,612,615,616,619,620,623],{},"Un événement ",[233,610,411],{}," marque le moment où le code a changé : un ",[233,613,614],{},"bench migrate"," sur le site\nWolf, une tâche Pilot, ou ",[233,617,618],{},"wolf-agent mark-deployment",". Les règles peuvent exiger un\ndéploiement récent (la règle prédéfinie ",[464,621,622],{},"502 spike after deployment","), et les incidents affichent\nle déploiement qui les a précédés, si bien que la chronologie se lit « les 502 ont commencé\n4 minutes après le déploiement de 01:47 ».",[188,625,627],{"id":626},"où-regarder","Où regarder",[629,630,631,641],"ul",{},[323,632,633,636,637,640],{},[224,634,635],{},"Wolf UI"," sur ",[233,638,639],{},"\u002Fwolf"," : vue d'ensemble, incidents, explorateurs, sécurité,\nsupervision. Pour les Wolf Users et les Wolf Managers.",[323,642,643,646,647,453],{},[224,644,645],{},"Desk"," : tous les DocTypes, la configuration, des rapports comme ",[224,648,649],{},"Wolf Incident Metrics",[651,652,653],"style",{},"html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-lig